-- title:
--   Irreducibility of the K(q)-fixed reduction representation
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a positive natural number, let $g$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform in the project's sense (a normalised eigenform, i.e. $a_1(g)=1$ with the multiplicativity and prime-power recursions for $\ell\nmid M$ and $\ell\mid M$, and such that no proper divisor $M'\mid M$ carries a normalised eigenform whose $\ell$-th coefficients agree with those of $g$ for all primes $\ell\nmid M$), let $q$ be a prime, and let $\Phi$ be a complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q})$ which is an adelic lift of $g$: left invariant under the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$, right invariant under the finite level-one subgroup attached to the ideal $(M)$ of $\mathcal{O}_\mathbb{Q}$, and satisfying $\Phi(h)=(g\mid_2 h_\infty)(i)$ for every $h$ whose finite part is trivial and whose archimedean component $h_\infty$ lies in $\mathrm{GL}_2^+(\mathbb{R})$. Assume that for all characters $\mu_1,\mu_2\colon\mathbb{Q}_q^\times\to\mathbb{C}^\times$ every $\mathbb{C}$-linear map from [`LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan Φ`](def/LocalNewvector_AdelicSpanCarrier.html#L82) to the principal-series space [`LocalNewvector.PSCarrier q μ₁ μ₂`](def/LocalNewvector_PrincipalSeriesCarrier.html#L173) commuting with the action of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$ is zero. Let $V$ be a complex vector space with a $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-action by $\mathbb{C}$-linear maps such that the submodule of vectors fixed by [`FLT.SmoothVectors.gl2CongruenceSubgroup q 1`](def/RepTheory_GL2CongruenceSubgroup.html#L181) — the subgroup of $x\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$ all of whose entries of $x-1$ and of $x^{-1}-1$ have norm at most $q^{-1}$ — is finite-dimensional, and let $f\colon V\to$ [`LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan Φ`](def/LocalNewvector_AdelicSpanCarrier.html#L82) be an injective $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-equivariant linear map whose range is the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the translates $x\cdot$[`LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan.self Φ`](def/LocalNewvector_AdelicSpanCarrier.html#L121), $x\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$. Then for the representation [`LocalNewvector.gl2ReductionRep q V`](def/LocalNewvector_ReductionFunctor.html#L187) of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ on that fixed submodule, every subrepresentation whose underlying submodule is non-zero has underlying submodule equal to the whole space. (Nontriviality of the space itself is not asserted.)
--
--   This is the irreducibility half of the local analysis at $q$ of the automorphic representation generated by an adelic lift of a newform: under the hypothesis that no non-zero equivariant map to a principal series exists, the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{F}_q)$-representation on the vectors fixed by the principal congruence subgroup of level $q$ has no proper non-zero invariant subspace. It feeds the subsequent identification of that representation as cuspidal of a definite type, used in determining the local behaviour at $q$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_IsNewform_gl2ReductionRep_toSubmodule_eq_top_of_ne_bot_of_forall_linearMap_psCarrier_eq_zero.lean

